WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.910
In 1987, a UN report defined
sustainable development:

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.270
meeting today's needs without harming
future generations' ability to meet theirs.

3
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.710
Industrialization raised incomes.

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.510
It also used up resources,
polluted air and water,

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.210
and warmed the climate.

6
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:24.150
In September 2015, UN member states agreed
17 Sustainable Development Goals, for

7
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.430
2030.

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.630
Count the money countries earn?

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.770
Ask leaders?

10
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.630
How can anyone tell if development
is becoming more sustainable?

11
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.530
In this mission, you'll meet four
problems that policies try to fix,

12
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.370
from mass consumption to climate change.

13
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.350
Then you'll test the goals on
small loans and city buses,

14
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.950
and judge the world's progress.

15
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.290
Your mission: find out how anyone can tell
if development is becoming more sustainable.
